# Playground ↔ theorem projection

The web playground (`theoremai-frontend`) is a **projection** of theorem. It must not invent profile, schema, protocol, tool, guardrail, or observability truths.

## Allowed frontend-owned policy

Only free-tier / host wiring in `src/lib/playground/playground-policy.ts` (free keys, free model ids, vault env). Canvas chrome (`expanded`, stubs) is UI-only.

## Must import from theorem

- Graph topology: `PROFILE_GRAPH`, `spineFacetsForProfileType`, `ProfileGraphFacetId`
- Field catalogs: `PROFILE_FIELDS`, `fieldMeta`, closed unions from `@theoremai/agents/schema`
- Defaults: omit empty optionals; rely on `resolveGuardrailPolicy` / `resolveObservabilityPolicy` / `defineProfile` (canary / sanitize / redact default **on**)
- Continue kinds: `CONTINUE_STOP_KINDS` / `ContinueStopKind` (not full `TURN_STOP_KINDS`); defaults `DEFAULT_ALLOW_CONTINUE`, `DEFAULT_AUTO_CONTINUE`

## Forbidden

- `FacetKind` / `SpineFacetKind` aliases are **forbidden**; use `ProfileGraphFacetId` from `@theoremai/agents/schema` directly — no local type aliases that duplicate the catalog
- Local spine lists that duplicate `PROFILE_GRAPH`
- Inventing `maxSteps`, `canary`, `sanitizeInput`, `redactSensitive`, `hasEgress`, inputs, or pin defaults that disagree with kernel omit semantics
- Seeding blank sync with `inputs.text: true`, `streamMode: 'sse'`, `maxOutputTokens`, `efforts`, image MIME lists, or speech `format: 'pcm'`
- Materializing `DEFAULT_ALLOW_CONTINUE` / `DEFAULT_AUTO_CONTINUE` into compiled profiles — empty UI lists omit those keys
- Painting omit as authored-on in chips (label `(default)` when unresolved)
- Porting playground convenience into kernel policy to "match the UI"
- Adding a profile section only in the frontend — add `PROFILE_FIELDS` + `PROFILE_GRAPH` in theorem first
